  "security_implications": "The rx timeout event (event_rx_timeout) is a potential security signal. If the timeout value is configured to zero while the feature is enabled, event_rx_timeout becomes permanently asserted, causing an interrupt storm. This can mask genuine timeout events, preventing detection of stalled communication, and may constitute a denial-of-service attack on the interrupt handler. The absence of a hardware guard against val==0 when enabled is a security concern.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "uart_core.sv:367-389"
  ],
